{
  "header": [
    "ECP-R7-P1 — rs-conformance's OBSERVER for included-entity hash validation.",
    "",
    "⛔⛔ THIS ITEM SCORES NOBODY, AND THAT IS A RULING RATHER THAN A LIMITATION OF THIS SUITE.",
    "§1.8 item 1 at 0.8.2.26, verbatim: \"A uniform verdict on an UNREFERENCED `included` entry is",
    "mechanism-shaped and MUST NOT be required [MUST] ... A conformance check MUST NOT assert a",
    "refusal on this input: asserting one votes mechanism (a) and makes (b) — which this item",
    "blesses — unimplementable.\"",
    "",
    "This probe's entry is unreferenced BY DESIGN — that is how §3.1's \"EACH included entity\" is",
    "reached rather than the weaker \"each one the handler uses\". So the very property that makes",
    "the probe reach the obligation is the property that makes its result unscoreable. The",
    "observation is recorded; `peer_attributable` is false on every row it produces.",
    "",
    "⚠ AND A GAP IN THE FORMATS, REPORTED RATHER THAN WORKED AROUND. Neither the item format's arm",
    "vocabulary (`conformant` · `negative-control` · `non-conformant`) nor the suite contract's",
    "verdict vocabulary (`PASS` · `WARN` · `FAIL` · `SKIP`) has a value meaning OBSERVED, NOT",
    "SCOREABLE. The arm below is `conformant` because §1.8 says both mechanisms ARE conformant on",
    "this input, which is the closest true statement available; the emitted verdict is `SKIP`,",
    "which [ADR-0012] counts as a failure — the wrong accounting for a row the SPECIFICATION",
    "forbids scoring. Both vocabularies need a witness value."
  ],

  "id": "ECP-R7-P1",
  "author": "rs-conformance",
  "class": "validate-peer check",
  "class_basis": [
    "GUIDE-CONFORMANCE §7.0's first class by construction — it is driven over the wire against a",
    "running peer — even though it yields no verdict. The class names WHAT DRIVES the item, not",
    "whether the item scores: an observation taken over the wire is still a wire observation, and",
    "filing it as anything else would misdescribe how it was obtained."
  ],
  "drives": [
    "entity-core-protocol/ECP-R7"
  ],
  "surface": "wire",
  "status": "disputed",
  "snapshot": "entity-core-protocol/v0.8.2.26",

  "preconditions": {
    "posture": "pre-handshake-floor",
    "connection_state": "not_established",
    "grants": "none — the vehicle is a hello on §4.2's sole pre-authorized path",
    "identities": "none",
    "connection_reuse": "none; a fresh TCP connection per arm"
  },

  "arm": [
    {
      "name": "both_mechanisms_are_conformant_observe_only",
      "kind": "conformant",
      "given": "a fresh TCP connection, no frames previously sent on it",
      "why": [
        "§3.1: \"On the wire, implementations MUST validate each included entity's content_hash",
        "individually per entity fidelity (§1.8).\" §6.5 orders it right after the root hash.",
        "",
        "⛔ BUT §1.8 ITEM 1 (0.8.2.26) FORBIDS ASSERTING A REFUSAL ON THIS PARTICULAR INPUT.",
        "Mechanism (a) inspects every entry as the map is accepted, so an unreferenced mis-keyed",
        "entry is refused. Mechanism (b) discards wire keys at the decode boundary, so it \"has no",
        "wire key to inspect and no entry to reach\" and the same input is \"NOT REPRESENTED AT ALL",
        "in the peer's decoded form\". \"Both are conformant, and the observable difference is a",
        "property of the mechanism rather than of the peer's correctness.\"",
        "",
        "⇒ THERE IS NO ACCEPT ROW AND NO REFUSE ROW. Writing one would vote for mechanism (a) and",
        "make mechanism (b) — which the specification blesses — unimplementable. The arm carries a",
        "witness table and nothing else, which is exactly what it is entitled to carry.",
        "",
        "WHAT WOULD MAKE IT SCOREABLE, stated so the next session does not re-derive it: the same",
        "obligation over a REFERENCED entry — one the peer must resolve to do its job — where both",
        "mechanisms must reach it, because mechanism (b) addresses entities by a `content_hash`",
        "validated under item 1's first half. ⬜ THAT PROBE IS NOT BUILT AND IS NOT A RENAME OF THIS",
        "ONE: a hello's `included` map may carry no entry the peer is OBLIGED to resolve, so the",
        "referenced surface may need an authenticated EXECUTE — which reintroduces the posture",
        "confound the hello was chosen to avoid. A real design question, left open rather than",
        "guessed at, and it is legitimate unclaimed work."
      ],
      "step": [
        {
          "op": "send_frame",
          "detail": "envelope { root: valid hello EXECUTE, included: { K => entity } } where the entity is a well-formed `primitive/any` the hello has no use for, K equals the hash of its ORIGINAL data, the entity's own carried content_hash also equals that hash, and the data was then changed — so the entry is both self-inconsistent and mis-keyed, and `content_hash({type,data})` of what arrives equals neither"
        },
        {
          "op": "read_frame",
          "detail": "one answer, or the absence of one"
        }
      ],
      "witness": [
        {
          "field": "observed_shape",
          "detail": "one of coded_response / bare_close / silent_drop / unreadable. RECORDED, NOT SCORED."
        },
        {
          "field": "status_and_code",
          "detail": "RECORDED, NOT SCORED. Of standing interest because §4.11's cause table row 3 pins `400 hash_mismatch` for resolution integrity while ENTITY-CBOR-ENCODING §5.4 scopes `400 non_canonical_ecf` to tag-policy violations, and this frame carries no tag. A peer answering `non_canonical_ecf` here is using a code for a condition it does not name — but on THIS input that observation is cohort data, not a verdict."
        },
        {
          "field": "root_and_params_validity",
          "detail": "both truthful, so any refusal is attributable to the included entry and not to ECP-R3's surface"
        },
        {
          "field": "closed_after_answer",
          "detail": "RECORDED, NEVER SCORED (§4.11)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "negative_control_wellformed_included_entry",
      "kind": "negative-control",
      "given": "a fresh TCP connection, no frames previously sent on it",
      "why": [
        "⛔ THE CONTROL RUNS EVEN THOUGH NOTHING IS SCORED, and that is deliberate. An observation",
        "taken against a peer that refuses everything is not an observation — it is noise recorded",
        "as cohort data, and cohort data is exactly what this row is FOR. Skipping the control",
        "because 'we are only witnessing' would put unattributable rows into the one output this",
        "item is allowed to produce.",
        "",
        "The corrected input carries the SAME included entity, correctly keyed and self-consistent."
      ],
      "step": [
        {
          "op": "send_frame",
          "detail": "the identical envelope with the included entity's data unmutated, so key == carried hash == content_hash({type,data})"
        },
        {
          "op": "read_frame",
          "detail": "one answer"
        }
      ],
      "accept": [
        {
          "outcome": "hello_answered",
          "status": 200,
          "detail": "EXECUTE_RESPONSE, 2xx — the peer accepts a well-formed envelope carrying a well-formed unreferenced entry"
        }
      ],
      "refuse": [
        {
          "outcome": "control_void",
          "detail": "anything else — the observation is discarded rather than recorded, and the row says COULD NOT LOOK"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],

  "measured": [
    "First run 2026-09-17 against `entity-core-go` (posture grants=bootstrap-default).",
    "",
    "CONTROL HELD — 200 EXECUTE_RESPONSE to the well-formed included entry, so the peer does not",
    "refuse an unreferenced entry as such.",
    "OBSERVED: `bare_close` on the mutated entry. NOT A VERDICT. Not routed as a peer finding.",
    "",
    "⭐ It is worth recording that this observation was reached by an instrument that shares no",
    "code, no codec, no crypto and no language with the instrument that recorded the same shape",
    "for this peer previously. Two instruments agreeing on an OBSERVATION is worth more than one,",
    "even where neither may score it."
  ]
}
